What is Multer?

Multer is an Express middleware used to handle file uploads. It processes multipart/form-data requests and provides uploaded files through req.file or req.files.

What is Buffer?

Buffer is a Node.js object used to store raw binary data in memory. It is commonly used when reading files, images, PDFs, or network data.

How are they used together?
Upload File
    ↓
Multer receives file
    ↓
File stored in disk/memory
    ↓
Convert file to Buffer
    ↓
Pass Buffer to libraries like pdf-parse
    ↓
Extract data